{"ocrText": "C O R R E S P O N D E N C E \n\u2022 C O R R E S P O N D E N C E \n\u2022 \nC O R R E S P O N D E N C E \nRELIGIOUS CHAOS? \nWould people knowing the \ntruth \nreally cause \nreligious \nchaos? \nI often hear it said that if the \npeople were to find out the \ntruth aPout UFOs and extrater-\nrestrials, society, as we know it, \nwould collapse into chaos due \nto the religious Peliefs of Pillions \nof us Peing shattered. \nThere's no douPt that if the \ngovernments of the world sud-\ndenly announced that there is \nintelligent extra-terrestrial life \nresiding on the Earth, it would \nbe a historical moment. But \nwould society really descend \ninto chaos? There would Pe \nsome concerned citizens, and \nI'm sure there would Pe a few \ngun toting rednecks getting \nready for Armageddon. But the \naforementioned rednecks look \nfor any excuse to Pehave like \nthat, \nrememPer \nY2K? They \nwere sitting in underground \nPunkers with 3 years worth of \ncanned food and \nenough \nguns and ammunition to effect \na \"regime change\" on a small \ncountry, while the rest of us \nwere out partying. I'm sure \nsome of them are still in those \nbunkers waiting for the radia-\ntion to suPside so they can \nemerge to do Pattle with the \nmutants. \nI'm sure in this day and age the \nlarge \nmajority of Christians \nPelieve that the BiPle isn't liter-\nally \ntrue. \nAnd \nrecently \na \nspokesman from the Vatican \nhas Peen quoted as saying \n\"extraterrestrials exist and are \nour Prothers\". Muslims also \nhave no proPlem with ET life. \nApparently it's all covered in \nthe Koran, \nDinosaurs are \nnever \nmen-\ntioned in the BiPle, or any other \nreligious texts to the Pest of my \nknowledge. Yet the discovery \nof \nmassive ancient \nreptile \nskeletons hasn't caused chaos \namongst the religious commu-\nnities. \nThe same \ncover-up \ncould have Peen applied to \nthem. You could just imagine \nsomeone digging u p their gar-\nden and finding a one metre \nlong skull. They then phone the \nnewspaper, \nreporters \narrive \ntake a few pictures, then it's all \nover the papers. Next thing you \nknow the \"Men in Black\" are \ngetting involved. People are \nthreatened, the skull is confis-\ncated, the story is dePunked \nand the man who found the \nskull is made out to Pe a \nlunatic or a hoaxer. We would \nhave an all-new culture of \nclaims \nand \ncounter-claims, \nresearchers and dePunkers, \nsightings and hoaxes. \nHumans are an \nincrediPle \nspecies. We know so much \naPout the universe we live in \nhaving Parely ventured away \nfrom our own tiny part of it. In \nonly one hundred years we \nhave gone from propeller dri-\nven planes to orPiting space \nstations and landing remote \nproPes on other planets. \nThere is still an infinite amount \nfor us to learn, Put I think we are \nready for the next step. \nMatt Johnson \nmj@genx4.net \nFACE IN BALL PLASMA? \nThe strangeness of this suPject \nhas long ceased to surprise \nme, therefore it was really only \nwith a mild shock when I saw \nwhat I perceived to Pe a head \nabove the presumed hand \nrails, of what now might Pe the \nsouPriquet of 'Fiery Chariot' \n(\"Engaging the Dragon', UFO \nMagazine, Jan. 2004, fig 5). \nThe head \nor \nper-\n\u00ab\nhaps \nit \nshould Pe \ncalled 'a \nface' \nis \napparent-\nly intent on looking down over \nthe side of its chariot, mayPe \npeering Pack at the humans \nthat were looking at it. It has the \nmien of a man. \nMr A.Calvert \nBarnet,Herts. \nOlSAPPOiTTH) \nI have read everything you \nhave puPlished aPout Crop \nCircles, and made my way \nthrough several Pooks includ-\ning Crop Circles - Signs of \nContact Py Colin Andrews. \nI am disappointed, for he \ngives us no answers. The Pook \nhas no storyline, just an accu-\nmulation of disjointed chap-\nters and several errors 'refer-\nring to Military Intelligence as \n'M-Fifteen', \nColin tells us firmly that Crop \nCircles appear only in cereal \ncrops, Put the Pook opens \nwith another so called expert, \nStephen J. Spignesi, telling us \nthat he wished for a circle of a \nspecific design and it \nappeared in a field of grass. \n(He didn't think to photograph \nit and it disappeared the next \nday,) \nColin then admits that many \ncircles appear in rapeseed \nfields. In succeeding para-\ngraphs he says foreign Circles \nhave different designs to the \nones found in the UK Put they \nare the same as ours. \nAEROSTAT SIGHTING \nRegarding the article \n'Snapshot from a cruise: An \nAerostat Sighting', \nUFO \nMagazine, Jan. 2004, page \n30. I can confirm that the \nphotos were indeed of the \ninfamous Aerostat Radar \nBalloon located at La \nParaguera, Lajas in Puerto \nRico. It is sited in a natural dip \nmaking it difficult to see when \ngrounded although it is just a \nfew hundred yards from the \nCariPPean Sea. When seen \naloft of course it is visible for \nmany miles. \nI have visited Puerto Rico a \nfew times mainly because of \nthe UFO situation in that coun-\ntry. Many of the local people \nquestion the government's \nreason for the Aerostat (to \ncomPat illegal drug trafficking) \nand wonder if its real purpose \nis to monitor the coming and \ngoing of the many UFOs \nreported and seen there. \nOn one of my trips to the \nisland I decided to visit and \nexplore the equally infamous \nThis matter of wishing or pre-\ncoggoing crop circle designs \nis nowhere properly examined; \nhe sights a drawing Py an \nAmerican woman which, he \nsays suPsequently turned up in \nnature yet the circle cited has \nalmost no similarity to the \ndrawing I \nI accept that one can easily \ndistinguish Petween genuine \nand hoaxed circles, so why \ndoes Colin's catalogue illus-\ntrate all the fakes without dis-\ntinction, and why are their sites \nnot identified? \nThis comes over as sheer slop-\npiness, and like so much of \nthe book it undermines Colin's \nclaims. In the end I am left \nwith two major questions; and, \nuntil these are answered, the \nwhole Crop circle thing \nremains a fuzzy puzzle. First, \nLaguna Cartagena where \nthere have been many UFOs \nreported entering and exiting \nthe water for many years. I \nwas told by a man and his \nwife who live near the lake \nthat on one very early morn-\ning they saw three differently \nshaped 'Ovni' flying aPove the \nlake area shining Peams on \nthe ground. \nwhy do some people deliPer-\nately fake crop circles? Are \nthey paid Py the government \n(see Colin's revelation aPout \nhow the British Army 'set-up' a \nPogus circle right in the mid-\ndle of his supposedly scientific \n'Operation BlackPird'), or is the \nCIA behind all the fakery? Or \nare they serving a secret alien \nbase on earth? \nMy second question is: what \ndo all these increasingly com-\nplex signs mean? Going from \nplain circles to the Julia set \nand other complex mathe-\nmatical and astronomical \ndesigns, what are the (pre-\nsumaPly alien) creators trying \nto tell us? \nIsn't it odd that, if these really \nare alien creations they should \nbe utterly incomprehensiPle? \nAnd why hasn't Colin Andrews \nor his many supporters tried to \nfigure out just what if anything \nthey mean? \nAs I said: I'm disappointed. \nCan anyone provide some \nproperly supported answers? \nWithout a single clue, the \nwhole topic seems pointless. \nKen Lake, Loughton, Essex \nI hired a Picycle and set off \nfrom my Pase in Parguera tak-\ning the short route through the \nhills. After 30 minutes or so I \nrealised I was lost. It was early \nmorning so on passing a \nhouse I stopped and asked for \ndirections. \nIt so happened the person I \nasked actually waked for the \npolice department. After initial \npleasantries were exchanged, \nin broken Spanish-English, I \nwas told that this person had \na close relative who worked \nfor NASA at the Aerostat instal-\nlation, and that they have 'lit-\ntle creatures' down therel \nWhen I asked for more infor-\nmation they told me it was \ndangerous to say more. (I am \nbeing purposefully vague in \ntheir description.) \nThe puzzle is why would NASA \noperate a Drug Trafficking \noPservation Palloon? Many \nPuerto Ricans are also puzzled \nPy the situation. \nM Prentis \nNottingham \nLEEDS CONFERENCE REFUNDS \nRefunds are being paid back in order of \nreceipt and although taking longer than first \nanticipated it is a continuing process. \nWe thank you for your patience and under-\nstanding over the last few difficult weeks and \nassure you that all refunds will be made. \nChristine Birdsall is dealing with the refunds \npersonally and can be contacted at this email \naddress orders@ufomag.co.uk \n78", "textLayer": [{"text": "C O R R E S P O N D E N C E", "x": 10.94, "y": 1.24, "w": 23.36, "h": 2.4, "fontSize": 13.1}, {"text": "\u2022", "x": 37.64, "y": 1.24, "w": 1.78, "h": 2.4, "fontSize": 16.9}, {"text": "C O R R E S P O N D E N C E", "x": 39.42, "y": 1.24, "w": 25.01, "h": 2.4, "fontSize": 13.1}, {"text": "\u2022", "x": 67.72, "y": 1.24, "w": 1.78, "h": 2.4, "fontSize": 16.9}, {"text": "C O R R E S P O N D E N C E", "x": 72.05, "y": 1.24, "w": 23.9, "h": 2.4, "fontSize": 13.1}, {"text": "RELIGIOUS CHAOS?", "x": 10.37, "y": 33.99, "w": 9.87, "h": 1.14, "fontSize": 8.0}, {"text": "Would people knowing the", "x": 7.23, "y": 36.13, "w": 16.36, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "truth", "x": 7.2, "y": 37.06, "w": 2.58, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "really cause", "x": 10.67, "y": 37.06, "w": 7.35, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "religious", "x": 19.04, "y": 37.06, "w": 4.53, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "chaos?", "x": 7.2, "y": 38.0, "w": 4.01, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "I often hear it said that if the", "x": 7.23, "y": 39.94, "w": 16.47, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "people were to find out the", "x": 7.23, "y": 40.87, "w": 16.36, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "truth aPout UFOs and extrater-", "x": 7.17, "y": 41.81, "w": 16.1, "h": 0.89, "fontSize": 6.7}, {"text": "restrials, 